WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.738
The New Year begins

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.972
with millions of Catholics

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:06.873
around the world

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.775
offering up prayers and mourning

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:09.843
for the loss of Pope

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.011
Emeritus Benedict,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.413
who died Saturday at the age of 95.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.348
His body is lying in state

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.683
at St Peter's Basilica,

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.019
where public viewing begins Monday.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:19.753
Earlier today,

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.755
Pope Francis presided over mass

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.922
in Vatican City,

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.125
sending prayers for his predecessor.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.493
Now let's go to CNN's

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.427
Frederik Pleitgen

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.462
live in Saint Peter's Square.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.398
Now the former pope left

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.900
a final letter published after his death,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.903
and in it he asked for forgiveness

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.371
from those who thought he had,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.906
quote, wronged

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.541
What can you tell us about this

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.810
letter and its meaning

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.346
Hi there, Paula.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.947
Well, it was a pretty lengthy letter

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.382
that he left behind to

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.717
to those in the Catholic Church,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.985
that which he oversaw.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.552
But then also,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.653
of course, to the many other people

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.421
that he dealt with

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.922
throughout his life as well.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.058
And that letter touches on many subjects

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:58.892
it touches on.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.125
You know,

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.093
when he was born, him

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.761
thanking his parents, thanking

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.896
the Catholic Church,

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.230
also his new home

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.398
as he put it here in Rome,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.367
but also Bavaria, which is, of course,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.435
where he comes from as well.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.502
But it was quite interesting.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.071
And that was also that segment

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.173
that we took a lot of note of as well,

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.541
where he asked for forgiveness

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.509
for those that he had wronged,

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.744
as he put it.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.412
And I want to read to you that passage

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.048
real quick, just so our viewers can hear.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:22.982
He said, quote,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:23.616
To all those

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.418
I have wronged in any way,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.487
I sincerely ask for forgiveness.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.322
But I said before to my compatriots,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.591
I now say to all those in the Catholic

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.492
Catholic Church

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.594
who have been entrusted to my service,

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.830
remain firm in the faith.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.398
Don't get confused.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.666
So obviously,

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.300
despite that,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.901
there may be people that he had wronged.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.336
He's asked for people

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.471
to to keep the faith

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.605
and to remain loyal

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.706
to the Catholic Church.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.040
Of course,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.807
one of the things

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.109
that we had been talking about

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.743
over the years reporting

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.545
when Pope Benedict was still in office,

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.013
was the fact that the Catholic Church

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.581
was dealing

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.116
with those sex abuse

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.351
scandals and generally abuse scandals

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.119
in that time.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:01:59.919
And many felt

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.720
that Pope Benedict

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.055
wasn't taking the action

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.323
that many felt that he should have.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.157
And in fact,

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.592
in the final months of his life,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.526
he acknowledged that

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.528
he had made mistakes in the past.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.530
This was pertaining to the time before

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.131
he was pope,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.166
when he was the archbishop of Munich.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.533
In the late

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.501
1970s

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.503
and early 1980s, acknowledging

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.971
that mistakes had taken place

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.072
there as well.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.940
So this could pertain to that,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.142
it could pertain to a lot of other things

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.442
as well.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.409
One of the other things

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.345
that we also picked up on that letter

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.679
was way at the end

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.213
where he said

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.214
that despite the fact

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.582
that he had many flaws

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.651
about him, that he had committed sins,

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.752
that he asked

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.387
humbly asked, as he put it,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.523
to be taken into God's heaven.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.257
Nevertheless,

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.925
so those were the final words really

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.561
in that letter left that he left behind.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.195
And something

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:42.595
of course,

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.897
that was very important here

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.533
in Rome, in the Vatican as well, Paula.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.467
And I want to go back

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.434
to one of the moments

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:48.935
that really the

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.970
significant moment of his tenure.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.938
He shocked the world's

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.007
1.2 billion Catholics by announcing

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.708
he was going to resign.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.943
How consequential

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.444
was that decision at the time?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.081
Well, I think it was I

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:02.815
think it was something

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.951
that was hugely consequential

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.052
because it was something

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.154
where he was the first pope to resign.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.156
And I think it was around 600 years.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:10.924
It was simply something

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:11.958
that was unheard of.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.792
But at the same time,

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.059
I think

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.093
many people also felt

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.428
that it was quite a strong step

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.030
because he was acknowledging

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.932
that he was not up to the task

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.867
of running the gigantic organization.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:21.901
And, you know, Paula,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.170
I was actually here in Saint Peter's

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.505
Square when he became pope.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.273
I saw him here on that balcony

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.374
when he took the reins

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.609
of the Catholic Church.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:32.612
He was already 78 years old at that time

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.713
and had already been

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.582
a hugely influential

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.416
cardinal here

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.483
in the Catholic Church

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.218
for decades

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:40.153
before that, since the early 1980s,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.521
there's a lot of people who say

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.223
that he was one of the most influential

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.591
people really in

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.360
a long time in the Catholic Church

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.962
and really ran the place

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.463
really the second one behind

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.532
Pope John Paul, the second at that time.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.601
But he was already 78 years old

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.468
when he took the reins

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.402
of the Catholic Church.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.704
And for the first couple of years

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:58.871
when he was pope

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.873
he did exude a lot of energy.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.942
I remember the World Youth Day in Cologne

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.244
in 2005

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.079
where hundreds of thousands of people

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:06.779
showed up.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.482
But you did notice that as time went on

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.384
some of these scandals came to light.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.452
There were a lot of issues

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.319
in the Catholic Church

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.388
that he simply lost a lot of that energy.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.156
He felt he was not up to it anymore.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.491
And I think a lot of people believe

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.726
that it was a pretty strong

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.060
step on his part

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.028
to then acknowledge

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.997
that he was not up to the task

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.898
of running this gigantic organization,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.234
which also needed some fresh leadership

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:28.668
at the top.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.169
At that point, many people felt as well.

